---
description: Conventional Commits and Conventional Branch naming
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commits

Conventional Commits: `<type>[optional scope][!]: <description>`

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`.
- Subject: lowercase, no trailing period.
- Note in the body when the change was not run on Windows.

# Branches

Conventional Branch: `<type>/<description>`, lowercase, hyphen-separated.

- Purpose types: `feature/` / `feat/`, `bugfix/` / `fix/`, `hotfix/`, `release/`, `chore/`.
- Docs or dependency change → `chore/`, not `docs/`.
- Agent-opened branches: prefix `cursor/`, `claude/`, `codex/`, `copilot/`, or `ai/`.
